CM_ "2018 Toyota 4Runner, DLC3 (OBD port) CAN bus at 500 kbit/s. Built from CANExplorer's field analysis of 24 logs (Dec 2025 - Oct 2026): layouts matching opendbc's toyota_rav4_2017/highlander_2017 DBCs bit for bit, and fits against the OBD-II PID replies the firmware polls (analysis/cx_obdref.py). See analysis/QUICK_REFERENCE.md for evidence and open candidates.";
CM_ SG_ 36 YAW_RATE "opendbc layout; deg/s scale as used by the firmware (KINEMATICS_*).";
CM_ SG_ 36 STEERING_TORQUE "opendbc layout; opendbc doubts this is steering torque.";
CM_ SG_ 36 ACCEL_Y "Lateral acceleration; firmware's fit against ABS PID 0x47: (raw - 512) * -0.002121 - 0.0126 g.";
CM_ SG_ 36 CHECKSUM "Toyota checksum: (id_hi + id_lo + DLC + bytes 0..DLC-2) & 0xFF. Holds in every frame of every log for 0x024, 0x025, 0x0B4, 0x1C4, 0x1D0, 0x237 and 0x2C1.";
CM_ SG_ 170 WHEEL_SPEED_FR "opendbc offset 67.67 reads exactly 0 at standstill (raw 6767); the firmware uses 6770, 0.03 km/h low.";
CM_ SG_ 452 RPM "Fits OBD PID 0x0C with r = 1.000 in 5 logs; same scale as the firmware (25/32) and opendbc's ENGINE_RPM.";
CM_ BO_ 464 "Not decoded; carries a Toyota checksum.";
CM_ SG_ 548 BRAKE_PRESSED "opendbc layout; found as a flag in 20 of 24 logs.";
CM_ BO_ 567 "Not decoded; carries a Toyota checksum.";
CM_ SG_ 705 GAS_PEDAL "opendbc layout; 0 = released.";
CM_ SG_ 865 THROTTLE_POSITION "Fit against OBD PID 0x11 (absolute throttle): r = 0.994-0.996 in 3 of 4 logs; the fourth matched byte 1 at r = 0.96.";
CM_ SG_ 976 VEHICLE_SPEED "Fits OBD PID 0x0D with r = 1.000, factor 1.00, in 4 logs; leads the PID reply by ~0.2 s.";
CM_ SG_ 1176 COOLANT_TEMP "Fit against OBD PID 0x05: factor 1.24-1.25, offset ~0, r = 0.998-1.000 in the two warm-up logs (2026-01-11, 2026-01-25). A zero offset is unusual for a temperature; check on a cold start.";
CM_ SG_ 1179 INTAKE_AIR_TEMP "Fit against OBD PID 0x0F: factor 1.24-1.25, offset ~0, r = 0.97-0.999 in 3 logs, 0.89 in one. Same zero-offset caveat as COOLANT_TEMP.";
